# shell: desktop
# board: ble
# The board's window over the air.  The board advertises, this host is the
# central, and the relay carries the connection to this desktop, which is
# listening as it does for a board that dials over IP: the drawing road
# rides the BLE link and the forms road, which is the shell's text, does
# not come with it.  This needs the board on the cable flashed with
# TIKU_LINK_BLE_ENABLE=1 TIKU_APPL_GUI=1 TIKU_APPL_GUI_BLE=1
# TIKU_APPL_DRAW_DEMO=1, plus TIKU_FLPR_ENABLE=1 on an nRF54L or
# TIKU_AMBIQ_POWER_PROBE=0 on the Apollo510B (for room), and the harness
# tells it to advertise and carries its link here (see run.sh's ble lane:
# BlueZ on Linux, tikuConsole's ble_relay on macOS).
wait 900
note the board's window is on the desktop, beside the fixture's folder
expect-windows 2
expect-title Board window
note the button counts: a press crosses the air and its redraw comes back
click 421 390
wait 60
expect-narrate Pressed 1 time
shot /tmp/trk_boardble.png
quit
